From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 23:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PC5: the controller starts a game from its launch window
 (Wine patch 0979)

Marvel's Spider-Man Remastered shows a launch window first (Play,
Settings, Quit) that reads the keyboard only: with the controller as the
game's XInput controller or DualSense, Cross and the D-pad did nothing
there, and the game could not be started without a USB keyboard. Its
window, of the class GameNxApp, now takes the dialog keys of Wine patch
0911 as a dialog box does, while it is smaller than the display: Cross is
Enter and the D-pad the arrows. The game's own window covers the display
and never gets them.
